/-!
# The triviality criterion over a local domain is not vacuous

A finite locally free module is only locally trivial, but on a scheme carrying a point whose
only open neighbourhood is the whole space — for instance the closed point of the spectrum of a
local ring, which lies in every nonempty open — the local trivialization at that point is
already global. For a module which is free of rank `r` the global sections are then computed by
additivity: the free module is a biproduct of `r` copies of `𝒪_X`, and global sections, being an
additive functor, turn that biproduct into the product `Γ(X, ⊤)^r`.

Over a local domain `A` this makes the identity of `Spec A` a concrete morphism satisfying every
field of `TrivialityInput`: every finite locally free module on `Spec A` is free, the zeroth
cohomology is the module of global sections and so is `A^r`, and the higher cohomology vanishes
because `Spec A` is affine, which kills the torsion terms in the comparison.

## Main results

The elided prefix is `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.FreenessOverDVR`.

* `isFreeOfFiniteRank_of_isFiniteLocallyFree`: a finite locally free module on a scheme with a
  point whose only open neighbourhood is the whole space is free of finite rank.
* `moduleGlobalSectionsFreeIso`: the global sections of the free module of rank `r` on a scheme
  `X` are `Γ(X, ⊤)^r`.
* `trivialityInput_id`: **the structure `TrivialityInput` is inhabited**, by the identity of
  `Spec A` over a local domain `A` and any element `π`.
* `geometricallyConnected_id`: the identity of a scheme has geometrically connected fibres. It
  is proper by Mathlib's instances, so the witness above is a morphism of the kind
  [Stacks, Tag 0EXF] is about.
* `exists_thickening_exponent_free_specId` and
  `exists_thickening_exponent_free_specPowerSeries`: the conclusion of [Stacks, Tag 0EXF] with
  no hypothesis left, for the identity of the spectrum of a discrete valuation ring and for the
  concrete discrete valuation ring `k⟦X⟧`.

## Implementation notes

The local trivialization is transported from the open subscheme `⊤` to `X` along the inverse of
`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.topIso`, using that restriction along an open immersion is a left
adjoint and so carries free modules to free modules.

The `A`-module structure on the cohomology of the identity of `Spec A` is restriction of scalars
along `A ≅ Γ(Spec A, ⊤)`, so the comparison with `A^r` is the inverse of that isomorphism applied
coordinatewise.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0EXF](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0EXF)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01XB](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01XB)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01C6](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01C6)
-/

